### 📌 Answer
Based strictly on the provided tender excerpt, the document explicitly prohibits bidders from contacting the purchase committee regarding bid matters after the bid opening until the contract is awarded. Therefore, the primary clarification focus should be on understanding the process for clarification of bids, as this is the only exception mentioned.

### 📄 Tender Evidence
33.b) Subject to the provisions concerning clarification of Bids, no Bidder shall contact the purchase committee on any matter relating to its bid from the time of the bid opening up to the time that the contract is awarded [Page 11].

### 💡 Consultant Interpretation
The tender imposes a strict restriction on post-bid contact with the purchase committee to maintain fairness and integrity of the evaluation process. The only permissible avenue for inquiry is through the "provisions concerning clarification of Bids." This implies that any necessary clarification must be submitted formally through the prescribed mechanism for bid clarification, rather than direct communication.

### 🎯 Recommended Action
Submit a formal clarification request addressing any ambiguities in the bidding documents, ensuring the request adheres strictly to the "provisions concerning clarification of Bids" mentioned in Clause 33.b. If the clarification process itself is not detailed elsewhere, a pre-bid query should seek confirmation on the exact procedure for submitting such clarifications.
