18. EXACT final response:
### 📌 Answer: Payment Terms & Warranty Commitments
- **Payment Milestones**: Payment within 30 days from the date of delivery,installation andacceptance certificate of concerned Department/Section/Purchase Section *(Page 1)*
- **Warranty Duration**: **5-Years Comprehensive Onsite Warranty**
- **Performance Security (PBG)**: Performance Security amounting to 3%of the purchase order value in favor of "The Director, NITK Surathkal"
- **Delay Penalties / Liquidated Damages**: Liquidated Damages for the delay, unless covered under Force Majeure conditions aforesaid, @ 1% per week or part of the week of the delayed period as pre-estimated damages not exceeding 5% of the contract value without any controversy/dispute of any sort whatsoever
- **Service Level Agreement (SLA)**: OEM on-site support with mandatory ticket resolution and spare parts availability.

### 📄 Tender Evidence
- Section: Commercial Terms & Conditions — Payments & Warranty, Page 1.
- Document: nitk_desktop.pdf

### 💡 Consultant Interpretation
- **Working Capital Strain**: Milestone payments subject to client inspection sign-offs can create 60-90 day cash flow gaps.
- **Warranty Costs**: Comprehensive warranty obligations require factoring OEM back-to-back warranty costs into the bid price.

### 🎯 Recommended Action
- Ensure OEM back-to-back warranty terms match or exceed the tender tenure.
- Clarify whether advance payment is available against bank guarantee during pre-bid queries.
========== FINAL RESPONSE END ==========

