### 📋 Tender Briefing: Supply, Installation, Testing, Commissioning of ANPR & IP Based CCTV Surveillance system of 09 Police District & 01 Commissionerate and Supply of Body Worn Camera & Night Vision Binocular under Inspector General of Police (North Bengal Region), West Bengal
Issued by **Webel Technology Limited** on behalf of **Inspector General of Police (North Bengal Region)** | Ref: `WTL/WBPNB/CCTV/26-27/046` | Submission Deadline: **22-09-2026**

#### 🏛️ What This Tender Is About
What this tender is about: Tender for Supply, Installation, Testing, Commissioning of ANPR & IP Based CCTV Surveillance system of 09 Police District & 01 Commissionerate and Supply of Body Worn Camera & Night Vision Binocular under Inspector General of Police (North Bengal Region), West Bengal under Webel Technology Limited (Execution Authority: Webel Technology Limited).

#### ⚙️ Procurement Opportunity & Scope
- **Main Technical Scope**: Implementation scope covering Supply, Installation, Testing, Commissioning of ANPR & IP Based CCTV Surveillance system of 09 Police District & 01 Commissionerate and Supply of Body Worn Camera & Night Vision Binocular under Inspector General of Police (North Bengal Region), West Bengal.
- **Estimated Tender Value**: Not disclosed in NIT; rates to be quoted in BOQ
- **Implementation Timeline**: Material Delivery: 60 days from the date of acceptance of contract | Commissioning: 90 days from the date of award | Overall Implementation: 180 Days from the date of issue of Work Order
- **Submission Deadline**: **22-09-2026**
- **Contract Duration & Warranty**: NOT FOUND (Warranty Period: 3 Years comprehensive warranty on all components for ANPR & CCTV System from the date of go-live of the system and 1 Year Warranty for Body Worn Camera & Night Vision Binocular from the date of supply)

#### 🎯 Key Eligibility Requirements
- **Minimum Turnover**: Minimum average annual turnover of not less than Rs. 12.00 Crore
- **Past Similar Experience**: The bidder shall have executed "Similar Nature" of single order an amount not less than Rs. 6.40 Crore OR
The bidder shall have executed "Similar Nature" of two orders, each amount not less than Rs. 4.00 Crore OR
The bidder shall have executed "Similar Nature" of three orders, each amount not less than Rs. 3.20 Crore
- **OEM Authorization (MAF)**: Mandatory Manufacturer Authorization Form (MAF) required from OEMs
- **Consortium / Joint Venture**: NOT FOUND

> ℹ️ **Bidder eligibility**: Not assessed — company credentials have not been provided. Click any suggested question below or ask me directly to evaluate your profile.

#### 💳 Key Financial Commitments
- **EMD / Bid Security**: Rs. 16,00,000.00 (Sixteen Lacs Only) (Tender Fee: Rs. 6000)
- **Performance Security (PBG)**: Performance Bank Guarantee (PBG) equivalent to 10% of the total contract value within three weeks from the date of receipt of Letter of Award/Order. The PBG should be valid for six month more than the warranty period.
- **Payment Terms**: Payment terms will be on back-to-back basis, i.e., payment will be made only on receipt of payment from customer. Scheduled Breakdown: 25% Mobilization Advance of total tender value on completion of selection process of Implementation Partner.; For ANPR & CCTV System --- 60% on completion of delivery of all active and passive equipment to site/district, as per delivery schedule agreed.; For Body Worn Camera & Night Vision Binocular --- 75% on completion of full delivery of materials including operational training.; For ANPR & CCTV System --- Balance 15% on completion of installation and commissioning in all sites.
- **Warranty Period**: 3 Years comprehensive warranty on all components for ANPR & CCTV System from the date of go-live of the system and 1 Year Warranty for Body Worn Camera & Night Vision Binocular from the date of supply
- **Delay Penalties / Liquidated Damages**: 17. LIQUIDATED DAMAGE Hardware: LD clause: I. 0.5% of the total Hardware bill value of this segment for every 7 days delay in meeting the delivery schedule II. The maximum deductible is capped at 5% of the total year wise SLA value. III. Vendor Termination Clause: - Termination possibility of MSI in the case of multiple cases of failure to meet SLA terms beyond monthly commitments for 6 continuous months

#### ⚠️ Critical Risks & Watchouts
- **🟠 Liquidated Damages and Strict Delivery Timeline**: Tight supply chain or OEM manufacturing lead times may trigger financial deductions (Page 4)

#### 🎯 Preliminary Bid Recommendation: Consultant Observation (⏰ Submission Deadline Passed)
> ⚠️ Bid Submission Deadline Lapsed (22-Sep-2026). The published submission deadline has expired. Participation is not recommended unless an active extension corrigendum is confirmed.
