### 📌 Answer: Key Technical Scope & Specifications
Implementation scope covering Design, Supply, Installation, Testing, Commissioning, Configuration, and Comprehensive Maintenance of an Enterprise-Grade Campus-Wide Wi-Fi Network, including all required Active and Passive Network Components, Controllers/Cloud Management, Network Security, Structured Cabling, Power.

> ℹ️ **Bidder compliance**: Not assessed — product proposal or OEM datasheets have not been provided.

**Computing & Processing Core**:
- **53**: Shall support DHCP relay, DHCP server/client, DNS/DDNS client. *(Page 5)*

**Networking, Ports & Connectivity**:
- **Section - I**: List of Dates, Tender Details and *(Page 2)*
- **Section-II**: Eligibility Criteria General Instruction, Scop of the works Etc. *(Page 2)*
- **Section-III**: General Terms & Conditions *(Page 2)*

**Software, Operating System & Security**:
- **Date and time for closing of submission.**: 17-11-2026 upto 10.30 AM *(Page 6)*

**Ancillary & Additional Specifications**:
- **Date and time of tender publication in the websites**: 22-10-2026 at 12.00 Noon *(Page 6)*
- **Data and time of Pre-Bid Meeting**: 12-11-2026 at. 3.00 PM *(Page 6)*
- **Date and time for opening of financial bid.**: 19-11-2026 at 10.00 AM *(Page 6)*

### 📄 Tender Evidence
- Section: Technical Specifications & Bill of Materials, Page 2.
- Document: Tendernotice_2 (5).pdf

### 💡 Consultant Interpretation
- **Datasheet Compliance**: Technical evaluators cross-check every parameter against published OEM datasheets; non-matching specs trigger rejection.

### 🎯 Recommended Action
- Obtain signed compliance letters and official technical datasheets from prospective OEMs.
- Prepare a clause-by-clause compliance matrix highlighting exact page numbers of OEM datasheets.
